nss-dp: honor AN8855 pause frames on the RD03v2 switch conduit

The switch-facing GMAC has no attached PHY and starts with receive flow
control disabled. Accelerated WiFi-to-LAN bursts then overflow the switch:
a 10-second run produced 464 FlowControlDrop increments and 464 TCP retries.
Temporarily setting only GMAC RX pause increased receiver throughput from
116 to 768 Mbit/s, with zero retries and zero added switch drops.

Use the existing HAL callback at each successful netdev open, including
NSS data-plane takeover, scoped to RD03v2 MAC2 without a PHY. Do not enable
TX pause or alter other boards. Full-image boot and local TCP were validated.

--- a/nss_dp_main.c
+++ b/nss_dp_main.c
@@ -482,6 +482,19 @@
 		phy_start(dp_priv->phydev);
 		phy_start_aneg(dp_priv->phydev);
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * The RD03v2 AN8855 CPU port sends pause frames when its LAN
+	 * egress queues fill. There is no PHY negotiation on this GMAC;
+	 * explicitly honor those frames on the switch-facing MAC only.
+	 * Apply after data-plane/HAL startup, including NSS takeover.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,mi-router-ax3000t-v2") &&
+	    dp_priv->macid == 2 && !dp_priv->phydev &&
+	    dp_priv->gmac_hal_ops->rxflowcontrol) {
+		dp_priv->gmac_hal_ops->rxflowcontrol(dp_priv->gmac_hal_ctx, true);
+		dp_priv->pause |= FLOW_CTRL_RX;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
